## Stack
FastAPI + SQLModel + SQLite + TanStack Router. Deployed on AdaLab.

## Commands
- Dev backend: `uv run uvicorn main:app --reload`
- Dev frontend: `cd frontend && pnpm run dev`
- Tests: `uv run pytest -q && cd frontend && pnpm run test`
- Lint: `uv run ruff check && cd frontend && pnpm run lint`
- Local container build: `docker compose -f compose.local.yml up --build`

## You MAY edit (no prompt)

- `app/api/routes/**` (except `main.py` and `deps.py`)
- `app/models/**` (except `base.py`; add new models, import them in `__init__.py`)
- `app/services/**`
- `app/schemas/**`
- `frontend/src/routes/**`
- `frontend/src/components/**`
- `frontend/src/api/*.ts` (except `client.ts`)
- `frontend/src/types/**`
- `frontend/src/styles/globals.css`
- `tests/**`
- `requirements.txt`, `pyproject.toml` (after edits, run `uv sync` then `uv export --no-hashes --no-dev --no-emit-project > requirements.txt` to keep them in sync)
- `frontend/package.json` (after edits, run `pnpm install` to refresh `pnpm-lock.yaml`)

## Sensitive but editable (you will be prompted)

- `.adalab/local_container_demo.json` — typical edits: add an environment variable, raise `max_ram` or `max_cpu`. Do NOT change `port`, `test_serving_port`, `uid`, `container_image_name`, `container_file`, or `build_context`.
- `frontend/src/styles/tokens.css` — you MAY add structural tokens (e.g. `--chart-color-1` through `--chart-color-8`, new `--space-*`, new `--radius-*`). Do NOT change `--color-primary`, `--color-secondary`, or `--color-accent`; those three are intended for per-demo human edits and should stay stable across feature work.

## You MUST NOT edit (blocked by .claude/hooks/protect_paths.py)

- `app/core/**`, `app/api/main.py`, `app/api/deps.py`, `app/models/base.py`, `main.py`
- `frontend/src/lib/basepath.ts`, `frontend/src/api/client.ts`, `frontend/src/main.tsx`, `frontend/vite.config.ts`
- `frontend/pnpm-lock.yaml`, `uv.lock` (autogenerated; touch package.json / pyproject.toml instead)
- `.adalab/app.json`, `.adalab/project.json`, `.vscode/**`
- `Containerfile`
- `.env*`, `*.pem`, `*.key`
- `.claude/hooks/**`, `.claude/settings.json`

If you believe a protected file must change, stop and explain why. Do not attempt workarounds.

## Adding dependencies

Adding a Python dep:
1. Edit `pyproject.toml` `dependencies = [...]`.
2. `uv sync` to install and refresh `uv.lock`.
3. `uv export --no-hashes --no-dev --no-emit-project > requirements.txt` (the Containerfile reads `requirements.txt`).
4. Run `/check`.

Adding a frontend dep:
1. Edit `frontend/package.json` `dependencies` or `devDependencies`.
2. `cd frontend && pnpm install` to refresh `pnpm-lock.yaml`.
3. Run `/check`.

You may also propose `uv add <pkg>` or `pnpm add <pkg>`; those commands are gated through `permissions.ask` and need human approval per call.

## Extending
Read `.claude/rules/feature-pattern.md` before adding a route. Read `.claude/rules/react-components.md` before adding a page. Read `TEMPLATE_TODO.md` for what's currently incomplete.

## Deployment
This app deploys to AdaLab via Test → Build → Deploy in the AdaLab VS Code extension. Do not invoke AdaLab commands yourself; the human drives the deploy.

## Database
SQLite at `./data/app.db`. Schema changes via `SQLModel.metadata.create_all()` on startup. Do not add Alembic.

## Workflow
1. Read the feature request and any relevant `.claude/rules/` files.
2. Propose a plan before editing multi-file work.
3. Implement, then run `/check`.
4. Invoke the `security-reviewer` agent before declaring done.
5. Do not commit. The human will review and commit.
